{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"hub","type":"text","text":"CAT11 — Course load and theory–practice gaps\nRQ3 · finding","x":140,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cases","type":"text","text":"Cases\nL1 L2 L3 L4 S1 S3 S6","x":-220,"y":-80,"width":300,"height":70,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"memo_group","type":"text","text":"**Memos** (7) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[L1M3]] — missing theory class breaks slide-only catch-up\n- [[L2M5]] — domain and course rhythm gate modeling uptake\n- [[L3M4]] — scaled labs: autonomy with timed rescue\n- [[L4M1]] — students arrive coding-first; value clicks late\n- [[S3M5]] — theory slides should carry complete examples\n- [[S1M6]] — incremental teaching would demystify diagrams\n- [[S6M3]] — examples and attendance carry abstraction norms","x":-380,"y":200,"width":520,"height":276,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"code_group","type":"text","text":"**Codes** (24) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[L1-C14]] — students miss theory and misread slides alone\n- [[L1-C15]] — lecturer does not require class attendance\n- [[L1-C22]] — heavy workload and continuous evaluation hurt attendance\n- [[L2-C17]] — domain understanding is the hardest learning condition\n- [[L2-C18]] — one shared project domain chosen for fairness\n- [[L2-C19]] — attendance and workload pull students away from class\n- [[L2-C22]] — modeling confined to one unit; low student interest\n- [[L3-C02]] — large cohort taught with multi-person teaching team\n- [[L3-C14]] — lab assistants break problems into smaller modeled pieces\n- [[L3-C15]] — autonomy first; whiteboard demo when majority stuck\n- [[L3-C16]] — lab supports learning but does not replace theory\n- [[L4-C01]] — broad prior course leaves little modelling time\n- [[L4-C02]] — lecturer sees students prefer coding over models\n- [[L4-C10]] — students grasp modelling value mainly at work\n- [[L4-C30]] — lecturer sees students undervalue modelling\n- [[L4-C31]] — lecturer sees compile mindset toward models\n- [[S1-C04]] — modelling useful up to a point then arbitrary\n- [[S1-C15]] — no remembered step-by-step teaching\n- [[S1-C24]] — incremental diagram teaching would demystify\n- [[S3-C02]] — MSP was the modelling-focused course\n- [[S3-C21]] — theory slides should show complete examples\n- [[S3-C22]] — repeated contact with notation builds familiarity\n- [[S6-C04]] — worked examples set acceptable abstraction levels\n- [[S6-C12]] — separate tools and missed tutorial blocked NFR progress","x":600,"y":200,"width":520,"height":752,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"explainer","type":"text","text":"What this means\n\nHeavy workload, skipped theory classes, and weak slides make practical modelling harder. The course setup gets in the way of practice.","x":80,"y":-360,"width":520,"height":150,"color":"1"}
	],
